Brief History of Seven Killings, making him the first Jamaican author to take home the U.K.'s most prestigious literary award. In addition to the Man Booker Prize, A Brief History of Seven ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.grinnell.edu/campus-life/arts-culture/writersgrinnell/distinguished-authors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d169\"},\"ref\":\"d169\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book is published by Juliet Mabey's Oneworld Publications, making it one of the two Booker-shortlisted titles last year released by an independent house. AOneworld has won the prize twice before, in consecutive years, with Marlon James' A Brief History of Seven Killings in 2015 and ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2024/07/the-uks-booker-prize-for-fiction-2024-longlist/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en}} | Longlist | Niall Williams | History of the Rain | Bloomsbury | *A. C. Grayling (chair) *Sarah Churchwell *Jonathan Bate *Dr Daniel Glaser *Dr Alastair Niven *Erica Wagner |\\n| 2015 | Winner | Marlon James | A Brief History of Seven Killings | Oneworld Publications | * Michael Wood ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d153\"},\"ref\":\"d153\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven Killings, winner 2015 by Marlon James Marlon James uses the attempted assassination of Bob Marley as the catalyst for a story spanning several decades, various locations and a huge cast of over seventy-five characters.\\n\\nDerbyshire-born author Sahota's novel depicts a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.panmacmillan.com/blogs/literary/our-all-time-favourite-man-booker-prize-winning-novels\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Spanning the 20th century, the novel is a philosophical exploration of human existence and history.\\n\\nThe End of Days won the 2015 Independent Foreign Fiction Prize and the Netherlands' European Literature Award.\\n\\nJenny Erpenbeck is a German novelist, playwright and director. Her books include Visitation, The End of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d170\"},\"ref\":\"d170\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven-Figure Book Advances\\ndate: 2018-05-08\\n---\\nA Brief History of Seven-Figure Book Advances\\n\\nFrom Tom Wolfe to Kristen Roupenian\\n\\nAh, book writing. For most people, it is not a viable (or at least not a reliable) source of income, but for ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/a-brief-history-of-seven-figure-book-advances/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d171\"},\"ref\":\"d171\",\"snippet\":\" ... I actually destroyed the manuscript, I even went on my friends computers and erased it.\\\" (Luckily, he found it again in his email.) In 2015, he won the Man Booker Prize for his third novel, A Brief History of Seven Killings.\\n\\nSteven Goldberg, The Inevitability of Patriarchy: 69 ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-most-rejected-books-of-all-time/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her latest collection is The Brief Reincarnation of a Girl (2015). She's been nominated for several awards including the 2014 Griffin Poetry Prize and has won the CBC Literary Prize for Poetry, the Bliss Carman, Pat Lowther, and … Read More\\n\\nJoan Naviyuk Kane\\n\\nJoan Naviyuk Kane is ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"2312265d4619a6d26111529f2e0a793c2a2cd8162f7ba2c6f4895ea3289385f6\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"bd40d1bfe1444d9a902dd526e2536b145a7081e892465a7b43eafcd799ea0459\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"A Brief History of Seven Killings publication date 2014 Booker Prize 2015\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... Raised in rural North Wales, he currently lives in New York where he is also a senior book editor and a volunteer E.M.T. crew chief.\\n\\nSpecial Guest\\n\\nAilah Ahmed is a publishing director at Penguin Random House where she publishes fiction by Chigozie Obioma, Lauren Groff ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... Farrell\\n*Karen Joy Fowler\\n*Linda Grant\\n*Abdulrazak Gurnah\\n*Sarah Hall\\n*Mohsin Hamid\\n*Shirley Hazzard\\n*Philip Hensher\\n*Mary Lawson\\n*David Lodge\\n*Patrick McCabe\\n*Colum McCann\\n*Tom McCarthy\\n*Shena Mackay\\n*Chigozie Obioma\\n*Michael Ondaatje\\n*Joseph O'Neill\\n*Tim Parks\\n*Caryl Phillips\\n*Julian Rathbone\\n*Mordecai Richler\\n*Arundhati Roy\\n*Bernice Rubens\\n*Donal ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d138\"},\"ref\":\"d138\",\"snippet\":\" ... Appiah argues that, unlike their counterparts who grew up facing the crudest forms of racial and colonial discrimination in the West and the Francophone subcontinent, the likes of S̩óyinká were \\\"children who were extracted from the traditional culture of their parents and grandparents and thrust into the ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d135\"},\"ref\":\"d135\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d134\"},\"ref\":\"d134\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book brilliantly explores the effects of slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): In this heartbreaking tale, four brothers in a small Nigerian town have their lives turned upside down ... \",\"title\":\"https://enkoeducation.com/the-must-read-in-african-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d140\"},\"ref\":\"d140\",\"snippet\":\" ... Born and raised in Queenstown, in South Africa's Eastern Cape, he now resides in Cape Town, where he has continued to nurture a far-ranging knowledge of Xhosa history and culture. His first novel, The Broken River Tent, reconstitutes the perspective of a real-life 19th-century ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2021/03/the-xhosa-literary-revival\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d133\"},\"ref\":\"d133\",\"snippet\":\" ... Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): The Fishermen (2015), An Orchestra of Minorities (2019)\\n* José Eduardo Agualusa (Angola): Rainy Season, Creole, The Book of Chameleons, My Father's Wives\\n* Ama Ata Aidoo (Ghana): Our Sister Killjoy (1977), Changes: a Love ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d137\"},\"ref\":\"d137\",\"snippet\":\" ... I, a great new African writer is asking these questions in a spare yet extraordinary novel about this bloody stain on human history.\\\"\\n\\n–Chigozie Obioma (The New York Times Book Review)\\n\\nFinalists:\\n\\nPeter Cameron, What Happens at Night (Catapult)\\n\\nAkwaeke Emezi, The Death of Vivek Oji (Riverhead)\\n\\nDanielle ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-award-winning-novels-of-2021/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d152\"},\"ref\":\"d152\",\"snippet\":\" ... Martin Literary Management and heads up adult fiction. Learn more.\\n\\nDigital media ventures\\n\\n- A new digital storytelling app, Alexander, focuses on shorts works by well-known authors. Alexander will launch with nonfiction works from authors such as Colum McCann, Xiaolu Guo, Chigozie Obioma, Carlo Rovelli, and Valeria Luiselli ... \",\"title\":\"https://janefriedman.com/new-publishers-agents-and-other-ventures-in-2020/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d136\"},\"ref\":\"d136\",\"snippet\":\" ... where she was a fellow from 2021-22. In 2022, she served as one of the judges of the International Booker Prize. She serves on the boards of Words Without Borders and the Hawthornden Foundation.\\n\\nBA, Harvard\\n\\nPhD, Yale\\n\\nShapiro Writing Center\\n\\nChigoze Obioma was born in Akure ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.wesleyan.edu/about/news/2023/09/wesleyan-welcomes-56-new-faculty-members-for-2023-24-academic-year.html\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"07c855b8f722a54f3728eb1189ba05225fac3e7c1d4dc12abcd992ee8646759c\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"f7cbf3b0beddf99f5ecdbff11e6977474c348558b69d062a965f072de86fecc4\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma grew up Akure childhood where raised\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_540d6ca740694153b08fea10"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure carefully. The key constraint is \"the award itself was originally created in the 2000s.\"\n\nThe Booker Prize was created in 1968/1969 — NOT the 2000s. So the Booker Prize doesn't fit. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005 (the 2000s). But The Fishermen was shortlisted for the Booker Prize, not the International Booker.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about a different award entirely. Let me think about awards created in the 2000s:\n- Man Booker International Prize (2005)\n- The Story Prize (2004)\n- Dylan Thomas Prize (2006)\n- Folio Prize (2014, no)\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole thing. Maybe Book A is NOT by Obioma. Let me reconsider the structure:\n- Book A: contender for an award created in the 2000s, translated into 25+ languages, published in the 2010s\n- In the year Book A was published, Book B won that award\n- Book B was released the preceding year\n- Author of Book B born in the same city where author of Book A grew up\n\nLet me reconsider the Man Booker International Prize. In 2015, it was won by Krasznahorkai (for body of work). But the puzzle says \"another book...won the very award.\" So the award must be for a single book. The International Booker Prize became a single-book award in 2016.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the award is the International Booker Prize (single book, from 2016). Let me check 2016 winner (The Vegetarian by Han Kang, translated by Deborah Smith). Was there a book published in 2016 that was a contender for the International Booker Prize, translated into 25+ languages, whose author grew up in Seoul (where Han Kang was born)?\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether the puzzle might be about the Man Booker International Prize and The Fishermen. Let me re-read: \"A book that was once a contender for an award, originally created in the 2000s (the award itself).\" Maybe \"contender\" doesn't mean shortlisted — maybe it means longlisted or just eligible. But The Fishermen was eligible for the Booker Prize, not the International.\n\nLet me step back and reconsider. Perhaps the award is NOT the Booker at all. Let me think about other awards created in the 2000s:\n- The Story Prize (2004)\n- Man Booker International Prize (2005)\n- Dylan Thomas Prize (2006)\n- Walter Scott Prize (2010)\n- Folio Prize (2014)\n\nLet me reconsider the Dylan Thomas Prize — created 2006. Or maybe I should reconsider whether the puzzle is about Obioma at all. Let me re-examine: the puzzle says \"translated into over twenty five languages.\" Obioma's books: 30 languages. That fits. \"In the 2010s, the year in which this book was published\" — The Fishermen 2015, An Orchestra of Minorities 2019.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the award is the Man Booker International Prize, and the puzzle is slightly loose about \"contender.\" But The Fishermen was NOT a contender for the International Booker. \n\nActually — wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about An Orchestra of Minorities (2019), and the award is the International Booker Prize. But An Orchestra of Minorities was written in English, so it's not eligible for the International Booker (which is for translated works). It was shortlisted for the Booker Prize 2019.\n\nLet me reconsider the Booker Prize 2019. The 2019 Booker Prize was won jointly by Margaret Atwood (The Testaments) and Bernardine Evaristo (Girl, Woman, Other). The Testaments was released in 2019. Hmm, \"released the preceding year\" doesn't fit.\n\nLet me reconsider the Booker Prize 2015. Winner: A Brief History of Seven Killings by Marlon James (2014). The Fishermen (2015) was shortlisted. So in 2015, the year The Fishermen was published, A Brief History of Seven Killings won the Booker Prize. But A Brief History of Seven Killings was published in 2014 (the preceding year)! That fits \"released the preceding year\"!\n\nBut the Booker Prize was created in 1968, not the 2000s. Unless... the puzzle considers the \"Man Booker Prize\" era (2002-2019) as \"created in the 2000s\"? The Man Group became sponsor in 2002. Hmm, that's a stretch but possible.\n\nNow: Marlon James (author of A Brief History of Seven Killings) — where was he born? And where did Obioma grow up? Obioma was born in Akure. Did he grow up in Akure? The puzzle says \"the city where the author of the initially mentioned book grew up.\" If Obioma grew up in Akure, and Marlon James was born in... Kingston, Jamaica. That doesn't match.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about a different pairing. Let me check Marlon James's birthplace and Obioma's upbringing more carefully. Actually, let me reconsider whether the \"award created in the 2000s\" could be the Man Booker Prize (renamed/rebranded in 2002). Let me verify Marlon James's birthplace.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Marlon James born Kingston Jamaica novelist biography\", \"Chigozie Obioma biography born Akure grew up childhood city\", \"A Brief History of Seven Killings Marlon James birthplace\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_380c739fe29a43a985e70cd3","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d167\"},\"ref\":\"d167\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Man on the Inside premieres 21 November on Netflix internationally\\n\\nGet Millie Black\\n\\nThe Jamaican-born novelist Marlon James, whose books include the Booker Prize winner A Brief History of Seven Killings (2014) and the Africa-set fantasy Black Leopard, Red Wolf (2019) created this crime series ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20241028-11-of-the-best-tv-shows-to-watch-this-november\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d172\"},\"ref\":\"d172\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven Killings, by Marlon James\\n\\nA nightmare symphony of crime that begins in 1970s Jamaica and never really leaves, even as the semi-historical plot leaves a surreal blood trail from a Bob Marley assassination attempt to crack-addled New York City. James' intoxicating ... \",\"title\":\"https://ew.com/books/2019/11/25/best-of-the-decade-top-10-fiction-books/?srsltid=AfmBOop0ufKoVqU4RELY55P6eS3L4rXFZLCabqalM9VtLWkrcVEOOLAO\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d163\"},\"ref\":\"d163\",\"snippet\":\" ... Marlon James\\n\\nWinner of the prestigious Booker Prize in 2015 for his book A Brief History of Seven Killings, Marlon James is a Jamaican novelist and teacher of literature at Macalester College in St. Paul, Minnesota. Both his parents worked with the Jamaican police. His mother, a detective ... \",\"title\":\"https://medium.com/@smilodon207/what-music-do-celebrated-authors-listen-to-while-they-write-39f04ddf7f28\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d173\"},\"ref\":\"d173\",\"snippet\":\" ... Old Bill\\\"), born in Murree, India,1888.\\n\\n• George Baker, British Actor, born in Bulgaria\\n\\n• James.G. Ballard, British Fiction Writer, born in Shanghai, China,1930.\\n\\n• Victor Barna, British Table-Tennis Champion, born in Hungary\\n\\n• Peter Simon Barnes, England Football International (22 Caps), born in Kingston, Jamaica, 1957.\\n\\n• Lord ... \",\"title\":\"https://peek-01.livejournal.com/64479.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d174\"},\"ref\":\"d174\",\"snippet\":\" ... Ward\\n\\n2011\\n\\nThe Round House\\n\\nLouise Erdrich\\n\\n2012\\n\\nAmericanah\\n\\nChimamanda Ngozi Adichie\\n\\n2013\\n\\nNevada\\n\\nImogen Binnie\\n\\n2013\\n\\nA Brief History of Seven Killings\\n\\nMarlon James\\n\\n2014\\n\\nFamily Life\\n\\nAkhil Sharma\\n\\n2014\\n\\nFates and Furies\\n\\nLauren Groff\\n\\n2015\\n\\nThe Fifth Season\\n\\nN. K. Jemisin\\n\\n2015\\n\\nThe Sellout\\n\\nPaul Beatty ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theatlantic.com/books/archive/2024/03/best-books-american-fiction/677479/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d160\"},\"ref\":\"d160\",\"snippet\":\" ... James in the 82nd minute to replace Je-Vaughn Watson. The former Kingston College schoolboy and Harbour View's under-21 player, entered the game and within minutes hit a sensational volleyed home from a right-sided cross from Ryan Johnson from inside the area to earn Jamaica ... \",\"title\":\"https://thereggaeboyz.com/news.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d175\"},\"ref\":\"d175\",\"snippet\":\" ... 107–123.\\n* Michener, James, A. 1989. Caribbean (especially Chap. XI. \\\"Martial Law in Jamaica\\\", pp. 403–442. Semi-fictional but mainly accurate). London: Secker & Warburg. .\\n* Morales Padrón, Francisco. 1953 2003. Spanish Jamaica. Kingston: Ian Randle Publishers.\\n* Nelson, Charmaine A. 2017. Slavery, geography and empire in nineteenth-century marine ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Jamaica\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d176\"},\"ref\":\"d176\",\"snippet\":\" ... Unreliable Memoirs, Falling Towards England and May Week Was in June\\n\\nClive James\\n\\nPicador, 2004\\n\\nThe Australian-born critic, poet, memoirist, novelist, travel writer and translator Clive James isn't as well known in America as he is in England, where he's lived most of his adult ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2019/06/26/books/best-memoirs.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previo