_fingerprint\":\"6b809e47e1db502e77c7253045668f9f5102dea365fc8a1561eaef8b96e83e21\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma biography born Akure grew up childhood city\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d164\"},\"ref\":\"d164\",\"snippet\":\" ... killed by the television industry, but these actors stayed afloat by adapting and accepting television roles.\\n\\nWhile there are some actors who may be older than the ones on this list, they have been retired for decades or had careers that lasted for a brief period of time ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oldest.org/culture/living-actors/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d107\"},\"ref\":\"d107\",\"snippet\":\" ... Lincoln in the Bardo - George Saunders (2017) - 10\\n\\nThe Narrow Road to the Deep North - Richard Flanagan (2014) - 9.5\\n\\nGirl, Woman, Other - Bernardine Evaristo (2019) - 9\\n\\nA Brief History of Seven Killings - Marlon James (2015) - 9\\n\\nBring Up The Bodies - Hilary Mantel (2012) - 8.5\\n\\nThe Sense ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d178\"},\"ref\":\"d178\",\"snippet\":\" ... Ruby by Cynthia Bond\\n\\n• Team Seven by Marcus Burke\\n\\n• Every Day Is for the Thief by Teju Cole\\n\\n• An Untamed State by Roxane Gay\\n\\n• Remedy For a Broken Angel by Toni Ann Johnson\\n\\n• A Brief History of Seven Killings by Marlon James\\n\\n• All Our Names by Dinaw Mengestu ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.culturalfront.org/2019/12/novels-by-black-writers-2000-2019.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d86\"},\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\" ... Marlon James\\n\\nMarlon James won the 2015 Man Booker Prize for Fiction for A Brief History of Seven Killings, making him the first Jamaican author to take home the U.K.'s most prestigious literary award. In addition to the Man Booker Prize, A Brief History of Seven ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.grinnell.edu/campus-life/arts-culture/writersgrinnell/distinguished-authors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d159\"},\"ref\":\"d159\",\"snippet\":\" ... Rocco Ritchie (born 2000)\\n\\n- Adopted as a single mother: David Banda (adopted 2006), Mercy James (adopted 2009), twins Esther and Stella Mwale (adopted 2017)\\n\\n- Age: 66\\n\\n- Birthplace: Michigan, USA, Bay City\\n\\nOzzy Osbourne has six children with two different women:\\n\\n- With Thelma Mayfair: Jessica (1972), Louis (1975), Elliot ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ranker.com/list/rock-stars-with-the-most-kids/celebrity-lists\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d179\"},\"ref\":\"d179\",\"snippet\":\" ... 78 times\\n\\nMarlon James, winner of this year's Man Booker Prize for A Brief History of Seven Killings, told the BBC he almost gave up writing after his first novel was rejected nearly 80 times. \\\"I did give it up. I actually destroyed the manuscript, I even ... \",\"title\":\"https://earlybirdbooks.com/15-famous-books-that-were-initially-rejected\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d153\"},\"ref\":\"d153\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven Killings, winner 2015 by Marlon James Marlon James uses the attempted assassination of Bob Marley as the catalyst for a story spanning several decades, various locations and a huge cast of over seventy-five characters.\\n\\nDerbyshire-born author Sahota's novel depicts a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.panmacmillan.com/blogs/literary/our-all-time-favourite-man-booker-prize-winning-novels\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d168\"},\"ref\":\"d168\",\"snippet\":\" ... Then the rising actor gave one of his most eerie performances to date in the psychological thriller The Killing of a Sacred Deer, also starring Colin Farrell and Nicole Kidman. Keoghan played Martin, a teenager with unknown sinister motives who befriends a surgeon and his family.\\n\\nThe movie ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/actors/a46180093/barry-keoghan\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d174\"},\"ref\":\"d174\",\"snippet\":\" ... the Bones\\n\\nJesmyn Ward\\n\\n2011\\n\\nThe Round House\\n\\nLouise Erdrich\\n\\n2012\\n\\nAmericanah\\n\\nChimamanda Ngozi Adichie\\n\\n2013\\n\\nNevada\\n\\nImogen Binnie\\n\\n2013\\n\\nA Brief History of Seven Killings\\n\\nMarlon James\\n\\n2014\\n\\nFamily Life\\n\\nAkhil Sharma\\n\\n2014\\n\\nFates and Furies\\n\\nLauren Groff\\n\\n2015\\n\\nThe Fifth Season\\n\\nN. K. Jemisin\\n\\n2015\\n\\nThe ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theatlantic.com/books/archive/2024/03/best-books-american-fiction/677479/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d180\"},\"ref\":\"d180\",\"snippet\":\" ... In addition to awards for acting, he also received a number of honorary awards recognizing his contributions to film.\\n\\n7 James Dean\\n\\n1931-1955\\n\\nBefore his death, James Dean had only starred in three films, all in the span of a year: John Steinbeck adaptation East of Eden ... \",\"title\":\"https://collider.com/movie-stars-1950s-iconic-ranked/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"b6f7285ebee3d1aecb702b9bfc84fc1a21ffcda866187e948f397c0f55d7199d\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"cb6f7600f7c50b0347e101ea495a7917ab9c8b4d6270fa88301b61210a9f2964\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"A Brief History of Seven Killings Marlon James birthplace\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_380c739fe29a43a985e70cd3"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure carefully. The key constraint is \"the award itself was originally created in the 2000s.\"\n\nThe Booker Prize was created in 1968/1969 — NOT the 2000s. So the Booker Prize doesn't fit. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005 (the 2000s). But The Fishermen was shortlisted for the Booker Prize, not the International Booker.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about a different award entirely. Let me think about awards created in the 2000s:\n- Man Booker International Prize (2005)\n- The Story Prize (2004)\n- Dylan Thomas Prize (2006)\n- Folio Prize (2014, no)\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole thing. Maybe Book A is NOT by Obioma. Let me reconsider the structure:\n- Book A: contender for an award created in the 2000s, translated into 25+ languages, published in the 2010s\n- In the year Book A was published, Book B won that award\n- Book B was released the preceding year\n- Author of Book B born in the same city where author of Book A grew up\n\nLet me reconsider the Man Booker International Prize. In 2015, it was won by Krasznahorkai (for body of work). But the puzzle says \"another book...won the very award.\" So the award must be for a single book. The International Booker Prize became a single-book award in 2016.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the award is the International Booker Prize (single book, from 2016). Let me check 2016 winner (The Vegetarian by Han Kang, translated by Deborah Smith). Was there a book published in 2016 that was a contender for the International Booker Prize, translated into 25+ languages, whose author grew up in Seoul (where Han Kang was born)?\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether the puzzle might be about the Man Booker International Prize and The Fishermen. Let me re-read: \"A book that was once a contender for an award, originally created in the 2000s (the award itself).\" Maybe \"contender\" doesn't mean shortlisted — maybe it means longlisted or just eligible. But The Fishermen was eligible for the Booker Prize, not the International.\n\nLet me step back and reconsider. Perhaps the award is NOT the Booker at all. Let me think about other awards created in the 2000s:\n- The Story Prize (2004)\n- Man Booker International Prize (2005)\n- Dylan Thomas Prize (2006)\n- Walter Scott Prize (2010)\n- Folio Prize (2014)\n\nLet me reconsider the Dylan Thomas Prize — created 2006. Or maybe I should reconsider whether the puzzle is about Obioma at all. Let me re-examine: the puzzle says \"translated into over twenty five languages.\" Obioma's books: 30 languages. That fits. \"In the 2010s, the year in which this book was published\" — The Fishermen 2015, An Orchestra of Minorities 2019.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the award is the Man Booker International Prize, and the puzzle is slightly loose about \"contender.\" But The Fishermen was NOT a contender for the International Booker. \n\nActually — wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about An Orchestra of Minorities (2019), and the award is the International Booker Prize. But An Orchestra of Minorities was written in English, so it's not eligible for the International Booker (which is for translated works). It was shortlisted for the Booker Prize 2019.\n\nLet me reconsider the Booker Prize 2019. The 2019 Booker Prize was won jointly by Margaret Atwood (The Testaments) and Bernardine Evaristo (Girl, Woman, Other). The Testaments was released in 2019. Hmm, \"released the preceding year\" doesn't fit.\n\nLet me reconsider the Booker Prize 2015. Winner: A Brief History of Seven Killings by Marlon James (2014). The Fishermen (2015) was shortlisted. So in 2015, the year The Fishermen was published, A Brief History of Seven Killings won the Booker Prize. But A Brief History of Seven Killings was published in 2014 (the preceding year)! That fits \"released the preceding year\"!\n\nBut the Booker Prize was created in 1968, not the 2000s. Unless... the puzzle considers the \"Man Booker Prize\" era (2002-2019) as \"created in the 2000s\"? The Man Group became sponsor in 2002. Hmm, that's a stretch but possible.\n\nNow: Marlon James (author of A Brief History of Seven Killings) — where was he born? And where did Obioma grow up? Obioma was born in Akure. Did he grow up in Akure? The puzzle says \"the city where the author of the initially mentioned book grew up.\" If Obioma grew up in Akure, and Marlon James was born in... Kingston, Jamaica. That doesn't match.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about a different pairing. Let me check Marlon James's birthplace and Obioma's upbringing more carefully. Actually, let me reconsider whether the \"award created in the 2000s\" could be the Man Booker Prize (renamed/rebranded in 2002). Let me verify Marlon James's birthplace.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Marlon James born Kingston Jamaica novelist biography\", \"Chigozie Obioma biography born Akure grew up childhood city\", \"A Brief History of Seven Killings Marlon James birthplace\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_5898357669454cf7b6c55339","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":true,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navi